## Generators

Each of these starts a new map {% own /%}.

{% card title="Random rooms" id="rooms" kind="Generator" %}
Scatter rectangles over a solid map, keep the ones that don’t overlap, and join them with corridors {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s47" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s48" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s49" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s50" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s51" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p5" /%}.

Stage `rooms`. The talk’s demo: `c01-rooms`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
repeat for a fixed number of attempts:
    pick a random rectangle
    carve it as a room, unless it comes within a tile of an earlier room
sort the rooms left to right
join each room to the one before it with an L-shaped corridor
```

The talk’s first technique is one that anyone who has done a roguelike development tutorial has seen {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s44" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s45" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s46" /%}. Its demo sorts the rooms by their left edge and joins each to the one before it, center to center {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57-L78" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Random rooms: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "rooms", demos: ["c01-rooms"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0001-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 30." key="rooms.add" at=1 of=30 %}
A random rectangle that comes within a tile of no room placed so far is carved as a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L46" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. It is room {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0008-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0008-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 8 of 30." key="rooms.discard" at=8 of=30 %}
This rectangle comes within a tile of a room already placed, so it is thrown away {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L53" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s54" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s55" /%}. Rooms placed so far: {% value %}7{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0014-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0014-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 14 of 30." key="rooms.add" at=14 of=30 %}
A random rectangle that comes within a tile of no room placed so far is carved as a room {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L46" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. It is room {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0021-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0021-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 21 of 30." key="rooms.sort" at=21 of=30 %}
The rooms are sorted by their left edge, the order they will be joined in {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L57-L69" /%}. Rooms to join: {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0022-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0022-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 22 of 30." key="rooms.corridor" at=22 of=30 %}
A corridor joins this room’s center to the center of the room before it: one run across and one up or down, in an order a coin flip picks {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. It is corridor {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c01-0030-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c01-0030-dark.png" alt="Random rooms, seed 1: the map at step 30 of 30." key="rooms.corridor" at=30 of=30 %}
A corridor joins this room’s center to the center of the room before it: one run across and one up or down, in an order a coin flip picks {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L67-L78" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L85-L101" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s57" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s58" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. It is corridor {% value %}9{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c01-rooms.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `attempts` (1 to 500; the talk’s: `20`) {% own /%}. How many rectangles are tried. The demo’s loop runs a fixed 20 times, and a rectangle that overlaps is discarded without another try {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L20-L54" /%}.
- `min_size` (1 to 30; the talk’s: `2`) {% own /%}. The smallest value a room’s width and height are drawn from {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c01-rooms/src/main.rs#L22-L27" /%}. A room covers one tile more than the value each way, because the rectangle type the demo uses includes both of its ends {% own /%}.
- `max_size` (1 to 30; the talk’s: `9`) {% own /%}. The largest such value. The demo writes it as an upper end of 10, which its random call leaves out {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

