{% /part %}

{% part title="What it combines with" %}
The talk’s demos that run it with other stages {% own /%}:

- [combine(bsp / cellular) → prefab](#) `c09`: two maps combined, with a prefab

The talk uses it as the left half of its combined map: a fortress that breaks out into caves {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Checked against the talk’s code" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#is-this-the-talks-technique) {% own-run values="list.checked.bsp" /%}:

- `c02-bsprooms`: 9 of 9 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Cellular automata" id="cellular" kind="Generator" %}
Random noise, with cell life rules applied to every tile again and again, until a natural-looking map comes out of it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s74" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s83" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s84" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p9" /%}.

Stage `cellular`. The talk’s demo: `c03-cellular`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
fill the map with random wall and floor
repeat for every pass, for all tiles inside the edge at once:
    walls = how many of the tile's eight neighbors are wall
    the tile becomes wall if walls is 0, or 5 or more
    otherwise it becomes floor
```

The talk gives the rule in three cases: no neighbors, a wall; one to four, empty; five or more, a wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. The neighbors its demo counts are walls, and a tile’s own state plays no part in what it becomes {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Cellular automata: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "cellular", demos: ["c03-cellular"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0001-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 11." key="cellular.noise" at=1 of=11 %}
Every tile, the map’s edge included, starts as wall with a {% value %}55{% /value %}% chance and as floor otherwise {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0002-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0002-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 2 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=2 of=11 %}
Every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its eight neighbors, reading a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. With five or more, or none, it becomes wall; with one to four, floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. This is pass {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0006-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0006-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 6 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=6 of=11 %}
Every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its eight neighbors, reading a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. With five or more, or none, it becomes wall; with one to four, floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. This is pass {% value %}5{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c03-0011-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c03-0011-dark.png" alt="Cellular automata, seed 1: the map at step 11 of 11." key="cellular.iterate" at=11 of=11 %}
Every tile inside the map’s outer ring counts the walls among its eight neighbors, reading a copy of the map made before the pass {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L40-L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s80" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. With five or more, or none, it becomes wall; with one to four, floor {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L61-L66" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s81" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s82" /%}. This is pass {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c03-cellular.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `wall_percent` (0 to 100; the talk’s: `55`) {% own /%}. The chance each tile starts as wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L19-L29" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
- `iterations` (0 to 100; the talk’s: `10`) {% own /%}. How many times the rule is applied to the whole map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L31-L34" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c03-cellular/src/main.rs#L56-L70" /%}.
{% /part %}

