{% /card %}

{% card title="Voronoi cells" id="voronoi" kind="Generator" %}
Scatter seed points and give every tile to its nearest seed: the map falls into cells {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s121" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s122" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s123" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s124" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s125" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s126" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p15" /%}.

Stage `voronoi`. The talk’s demo: `c08a-voronoi`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
scatter seed points over the map
each tile joins its nearest seed, by a chosen measure of distance
a tile is on an edge where its right or lower neighbor belongs to another seed
edges become walls (the talk's demo), or roads (our rule)
```

The first use the talk gives for the cells is to find their edges and place walls there {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s136" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s137" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s138" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p16" /%}. Its demo draws the edges as `#`, the glyph its shared map code treats as open {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L113" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. We follow the talk’s words and make them walls {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Voronoi cells, Roads (our rule): seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "voronoi", demos: ["c08a-voronoi", "roads"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0001-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 5." key="voronoi.seeds" at=1 of=5 %}
Seed points are scattered at random inside the map’s outer ring {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L21-L26" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s121" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s122" /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0002-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0002-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 2 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.pythagoras" at=2 of=5 %}
Every tile joins its nearest seed, measured in a straight line, and the boundaries come out fairly smooth {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L36-L52" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s125" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s126" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s130" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0003-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0003-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 3 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.manhattan" at=3 of=5 %}
The same with Manhattan distance, the blocks across plus the blocks down: the boundaries turn sharp-edged {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L57-L73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s131" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s132" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s133" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0004-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0004-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 4 of 5." key="voronoi.membership.chebyshev" at=4 of=5 %}
The same with Chebyshev distance, which the talk places somewhere between the other two {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L77-L93" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s134" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s135" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c08a-0005-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c08a-0005-dark.png" alt="Voronoi cells, seed 1: the map at step 5 of 5." key="voronoi.walls" at=5 of=5 %}
A tile inside the map’s outer ring becomes a boundary wall when the tile to its right or the tile below it belongs to another seed {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L113" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s137" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s138" /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/roads-0005-light.png" dark="assets/steps/roads-0005-dark.png" alt="Roads (our rule), seed 1: the map at step 5 of 5." key="voronoi.roads" at=5 of=5 %}
Our own rule, for a use the talk describes without code: the boundaries become road and the cells solid, and a tile is road when its right, lower or lower-right neighbor belongs to another seed {% own /%}. Seeds: {% value %}16{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c08a-voronoi.json`, `map-lab build recipes/own/voronoi-roads.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `seeds` (1 to 200; the talk’s: `16`) {% own /%}. How many seed points are scattered {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L21-L27" /%}.
- `metric` (`pythagoras`, `manhattan`, `chebyshev`; the talk’s: `pythagoras`) {% own /%}. The distance that decides a tile’s nearest seed. The demo shows all three and builds its walls from the straight-line one {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L36-L53" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L57-L73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L77-L93" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08a-voronoi/src/main.rs#L96-L110" /%}.
- `edges` (`walls`, `roads`; the talk’s: `walls`) {% own /%}. `walls` is the talk’s demo. `roads` is our own rule for the roads the talk describes: the edges become floor and the cells solid, and a tile is also on an edge when its lower-right neighbor belongs to another seed {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it produces, measured" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.voronoi" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: Voronoi cells" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Voronoi cells (c08a)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.836, 0.829 to 0.842 {% mark p10=0.829 median=0.836 p90=0.842 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
* 16, 16 to 17 {% mark p10=16 median=16 p90=17 unit="seeds" to=60 trait="regions" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="regions" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Dead ends](#our-definitions)
* 15, 12 to 20 {% mark p10=12 median=15 p90=20 unit="seeds" to=140 trait="dead_ends" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="dead_ends" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Corridor ratio](#our-definitions)
* 0.005, 0.004 to 0.007 {% mark p10=0.004 median=0.005 p90=0.007 unit="seeds" to=0.4 trait="corridor_ratio" series="c08a-voronoi" /%}
* {% now trait="corridor_ratio" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Path](#our-definitions)
* –
* {% now trait="path" digits=0 /%}
{% /table %}

Walls seal each cell: a map has 16 regions at the median, and the probe finds no path on any of the 200 seeds {% own-run values="c08a.regions.median c08a.path.nulls" /%}. The talk’s next use for cells is placing monsters: together in one cell, or kept apart in distant ones {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s139" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s140" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s141" /%}. Our roads are one region on 181 of 200 seeds and two on the other 19 {% own-run values="roads.regions.is1 roads.regions.is2" /%}. Without the lower-right neighbor, an edge that runs down and to the left touches itself only at corners, which seals a cell but can’t be walked {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

