{% part title="What it combines with" %}
None of the talk’s demos runs it with another stage {% own /%}.

In the questions after the talk, its author suggests mixing several noise maps together, or running an erosion simulation over one {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s307" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s308" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s309" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s310" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s311" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s312" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s313" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s314" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s322" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s323" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s324" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Checked against the talk’s code" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#is-this-the-talks-technique) {% own-run values="list.checked.noise" /%}:

- `c10-perlin`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c11-overworld`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c12-noisezoom`: 10 of 10 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
- `c13-double-noise`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

## Shaping and combining

These change a map that another stage made, or join two {% own /%}.

{% card title="Erosion by aggregation" id="dla-erode" kind="Shaping" %}
Fire particles at a finished map and let them eat at its walls, so it looks more organic and keeps its structure {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s191" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s192" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s193" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s194" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s195" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s196" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s197" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p21" /%}.

Stage `dla-erode`. The talk’s demo: `c08-dla-erosion`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
start from a finished map
repeat for a number of particles:
    start a particle on a random open tile
    step at random until it stands on rock
    dig that tile
```

Each particle digs exactly one tile: the first rock its walk reaches from inside the open area {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c08-dla-erosion/src/main.rs#L86-L128" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Rooms, eroded: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "dla-erode", demos: ["c08-dla-erosion"]} %}
