{% /card %}

{% card title="Combining two maps" id="combine" kind="Shaping" %}
Two maps, each from a pipeline of its own, joined into one: the talk’s point that a map rarely needs just one technique {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s179" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s180" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p20" /%}.

Stage `combine`. The talk’s demo: `c09-combination`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
build the first input on a map of its own
build the second input on a map of its own
the result's left half is the first map's, and its right half the second's
```

The talk’s example is a fortress of rooms on the left that breaks out into caves on the right {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}. Its demo copies the halves column for column and joins nothing {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L100-L114" /%}. The talk’s author then adds a prefab of fortifications down the middle {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s186" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s187" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s188" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through BSP + caves + spine: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "combine", demos: ["c09-combination"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c09-0001-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c09-0001-dark.png" alt="BSP + caves + spine, seed 1: the map at step 1 of 54." key="combine.input" at=1 of=54 %}
Each input is built on a map of its own: in the talk’s demo, rooms in subdivided space, then a cellular automata map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L41-L79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L82-L97" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}. This is input {% value %}1{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c09-0046-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c09-0046-dark.png" alt="BSP + caves + spine, seed 1: the map at step 46 of 54." at=46 of=54 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c09-0047-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c09-0047-dark.png" alt="BSP + caves + spine, seed 1: the map at step 47 of 54." key="combine.input" at=47 of=54 %}
Each input is built on a map of its own: in the talk’s demo, rooms in subdivided space, then a cellular automata map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L41-L79" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L82-L97" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s181" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s182" /%}. This is input {% value %}2{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c09-0052-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c09-0052-dark.png" alt="BSP + caves + spine, seed 1: the map at step 52 of 54." at=52 of=54 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c09-0053-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c09-0053-dark.png" alt="BSP + caves + spine, seed 1: the map at step 53 of 54." key="combine.halves" at=53 of=54 %}
The left half of the map is copied from the first input and the right half from the second, column for column, and nothing joins them {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c09-combination/src/main.rs#L100-L114" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s183" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s184" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s185" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c09-combination.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
The stage’s two inputs are pipelines of their own. In the lab’s strip they are the left row and the right row, and a stage can be added to either {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

