{% /card %}

## Analysis and placement

These read a map: what can be reached, where to start and end, and what lies near the way between {% own /%}. The talk builds its next set of algorithms on Dijkstra maps {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s209" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s210" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s211" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s212" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s213" /%}.

{% card title="Culling what can’t be reached" id="cull" kind="Analysis" %}
Find the parts of a map that can’t be reached, then delete them or put them to use {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s222" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s223" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s230" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s231" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s232" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s233" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s234" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p24" /%}.

Stage `cull`. The talk’s demo: `c16-unreachable`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
find the open tile nearest the center
flood outward from it, counting steps: a Dijkstra map
every open tile the flood never reached is unreachable
mark those tiles, or turn them to wall
```

The talk builds this on Dijkstra maps: from a starting point, every walkable tile gets the number of steps to it, and a tile left at the sentinel value can’t be reached {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s214" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s215" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s216" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s217" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s218" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s219" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s220" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s221" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p23" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, unreachable marked: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "cull", demos: ["c16-unreachable"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c16-0011-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c16-0011-dark.png" alt="Caves, unreachable marked, seed 1: the map at step 11 of 13." at=11 of=13 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c16-0012-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c16-0012-dark.png" alt="Caves, unreachable marked, seed 1: the map at step 12 of 13." key="cull.center" at=12 of=13 %}
The open tile nearest the center of the map is found {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c16-unreachable/src/main.rs#L36-L54" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s224" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c16-0013-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c16-0013-dark.png" alt="Caves, unreachable marked, seed 1: the map at step 13 of 13." key="cull.marked" at=13 of=13 %}
A Dijkstra map from that tile gives every tile it can walk to a distance. Open tiles left without one can’t be reached, and are marked {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c16-unreachable/src/main.rs#L62-L73" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s225" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s226" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s227" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s228" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s229" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. Tiles marked: {% value %}14{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c16-unreachable.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `mode` (`remove`, `mark`; the talk’s: `mark`) {% own /%}. `mark` shows the unreachable tiles and leaves them, as the demo `c16-unreachable` does {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c16-unreachable/src/main.rs#L62-L73" /%}. `remove` turns them to wall, as the demo `c17-starting-left` does before it places its start {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L54-L94" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it produces, measured" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.cull" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: Culling what can’t be reached" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Caves, unreachable marked (c16)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.637, 0.608 to 0.665 {% mark p10=0.608 median=0.637 p90=0.665 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c16-unreachable" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
* 17, 11 to 23 {% mark p10=11 median=17 p90=23 unit="seeds" to=60 trait="regions" series="c16-unreachable" /%}
* {% now trait="regions" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Dead ends](#our-definitions)
* 67, 57 to 83 {% mark p10=57 median=67 p90=83 unit="seeds" to=140 trait="dead_ends" series="c16-unreachable" /%}
* {% now trait="dead_ends" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Corridor ratio](#our-definitions)
* 0.131, 0.116 to 0.149 {% mark p10=0.116 median=0.131 p90=0.149 unit="seeds" to=0.4 trait="corridor_ratio" series="c16-unreachable" /%}
