* {% now trait="path" digits=0 /%}
{% /table %}

Marking changes no tile, so this is the cave map’s own row {% own /%}. With `remove`, as in the talk’s next demo, a map is 1 region on every seed {% own-run values="c17.regions.max" /%}. What the cull costs varies: the floor share after it runs from 0.424 to 0.694, where the caves before it never fell below 0.559 {% own-run values="c17.floor_share.min c17.floor_share.max c03.floor_share.min" /%}. The talk warns of the extreme case, a map with only two tiles you can walk on, which culling before picking a start avoids {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s236" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s237" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s238" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s239" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s240" /%}.
{% /part %}

