{% part title="What it combines with" %}
The talk’s demos that run it with other stages {% own /%}:

- [cellular → cull](#recipe=eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJtYXAtbGFiLXJlY2lwZS8xIiwicGlwZWxpbmUiOlt7InN0YWdlIjoiY2VsbHVsYXIiLCJ3YWxsX3BlcmNlbnQiOjU1LCJpdGVyYXRpb25zIjoxMH0seyJzdGFnZSI6ImN1bGwiLCJmcm9tIjoiY2VudGVyIiwibW9kZSI6Im1hcmsifV0sInNlZWQiOjF9) `c16`: finding unreachable areas
- [cellular → cull → start](#recipe=eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJtYXAtbGFiLXJlY2lwZS8xIiwicGlwZWxpbmUiOlt7InN0YWdlIjoiY2VsbHVsYXIiLCJ3YWxsX3BlcmNlbnQiOjU1LCJpdGVyYXRpb25zIjoxMH0seyJzdGFnZSI6ImN1bGwiLCJmcm9tIjoiY2VudGVyIiwibW9kZSI6InJlbW92ZSJ9LHsic3RhZ2UiOiJzdGFydCIsImF0IjoibGVmdCJ9XSwic2VlZCI6MX0) `c17`: a start on the left
- [cellular → cull → start → exit](#recipe=eyJmb3JtYXQiOiJtYXAtbGFiLXJlY2lwZS8xIiwicGlwZWxpbmUiOlt7InN0YWdlIjoiY2VsbHVsYXIiLCJ3YWxsX3BlcmNlbnQiOjU1LCJpdGVyYXRpb25zIjoxMH0seyJzdGFnZSI6ImN1bGwiLCJmcm9tIjoiY2VudGVyIiwibW9kZSI6InJlbW92ZSJ9LHsic3RhZ2UiOiJzdGFydCIsImF0IjoibGVmdCJ9LHsic3RhZ2UiOiJleGl0IiwiYXQiOiJyaWdodCJ9XSwic2VlZCI6MX0) `c18`: an exit on the right
- [cellular → cull → start → exit](#) `c19`: the least accessible exit
- [cellular → cull → start → exit → hot-path](#) `c20`: the hot path

The talk culls before it picks a start, so the player can’t be placed somewhere they can’t get out of {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s236" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s237" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Checked against the talk’s code" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#is-this-the-talks-technique) {% own-run values="list.checked.cull" /%}:

- `c16-unreachable`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Placing the start" id="start" kind="Analysis" %}
Decide where the start should be, then put it on the nearest tile that is open {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s241" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s242" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s243" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p25" /%}.

Stage `start`. The talk’s demo: `c17-starting-left`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
choose a desired point: the middle of the left edge, or the center
the start is the open tile nearest it, in a straight line
```

The demo measures every open tile’s straight-line distance to the desired point and takes the smallest {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L69-L86" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. It does so on a map already culled, so the start can walk to everything that is left {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L34-L67" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s236" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s237" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, culled: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "start", demos: ["c17-starting-left"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c17-0013-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c17-0013-dark.png" alt="Caves, culled, seed 1: the map at step 13 of 15." at=13 of=15 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c17-0014-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c17-0014-dark.png" alt="Caves, culled, seed 1: the map at step 14 of 15." key="start.desired" at=14 of=15 %}
Where the start should be: in the talk’s demos, the middle of the left edge or the center of the map {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L70" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L69" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s241" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s242" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c17-0015-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c17-0015-dark.png" alt="Caves, culled, seed 1: the map at step 15 of 15." key="start.placed" at=15 of=15 %}
The start goes on the open tile nearest that point in a straight line {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L71-L86" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s242" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s243" /%}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c17-starting-left.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `at` (`left`, `center`; the talk’s: `left`) {% own /%}. `left` is the middle of the left edge {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c17-starting-left/src/main.rs#L70" /%}. `center` is the middle of the map, as in the demo `c19-ending-dijkstra` {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L69" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it produces, measured" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.start" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: Placing the start" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Caves, culled (c17)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.627, 0.590 to 0.660 {% mark p10=0.59 median=0.627 p90=0.66 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c17-starting-left" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
* 1, 1 to 1 {% mark p10=1 median=1 p90=1 unit="seeds" to=60 trait="regions" series="c17-starting-left" /%}
* {% now trait="regions" digits=0 /%}
