{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Placing the exit" id="exit" kind="Analysis" %}
Put the exit near a point you choose, or let a Dijkstra map find the tile that is farthest from the start {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s244" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s245" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s246" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s247" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s248" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p26" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p27" /%}.

Stage `exit`. The talk’s demos: `c18-ending-right`, `c19-ending-dijkstra`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
right:    the exit is the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge
farthest: flood outward from the start, counting steps;
          the exit is the reachable tile with the highest count
then find the route from the start to the exit
```

The talk calls the second the least accessible part of the map, for when you really dislike your player {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}. With a start in the middle it calls putting the exit there a really bad idea, and a great way to hide something {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s251" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s252" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s253" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s254" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s255" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s256" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, exit at right, Caves, exit farthest, Exit without a cull (ours): seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "exit", demos: ["c18-ending-right", "c19-ending-dijkstra", "nocull"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c18-0015-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c18-0015-dark.png" alt="Caves, exit at right, seed 1: the map at step 15 of 16." at=15 of=16 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c18-0016-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c18-0016-dark.png" alt="Caves, exit at right, seed 1: the map at step 16 of 16." key="exit.placed" at=16 of=16 %}
The exit goes on the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge, and the route from the start to it is found {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L92-L111" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s247" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s248" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. Steps on the shortest route: {% value %}105{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c19-0016-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c19-0016-dark.png" alt="Caves, exit farthest, seed 1: the map at step 16 of 16." key="exit.placed#c19-ending-dijkstra" at=16 of=16 %}
A Dijkstra map from the start gives every tile it can reach its walking distance, and the exit goes on the tile with the largest: the least accessible one {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L92-L103" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s249" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s250" /%}. Steps on the shortest route: {% value %}68{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/nocull-0014-light.png" dark="assets/steps/nocull-0014-dark.png" alt="Exit without a cull (ours), seed 0: the map at step 14 of 14." key="exit.no-path" at=14 of=14 %}
The exit is placed, but no route reaches it from the start: without a cull, the two can land in separate caves {% own /%}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c18-ending-right.json`, `map-lab build recipes/c19-ending-dijkstra.json`, `map-lab build recipes/own/exit-without-cull.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `at` (`right`, `farthest`; the talk’s: `right` in `c18`, `farthest` in `c19`) {% own /%}. `right` takes the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c18-ending-right/src/main.rs#L92-L109" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. `farthest` takes the tile with the largest walking distance from the start {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c19-ending-dijkstra/src/main.rs#L92-L101" /%}.
{% /part %}

