{% /card %}

{% card title="The hot path" id="hot-path" kind="Analysis" %}
Everything close to the best route through a map, though not necessarily on it {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s257" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s258" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s259" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p28" /%}.

Stage `hot-path`. The talk’s demo: `c20-hot-path`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
find the route from the start to the exit
flood outward from every tile of the route at once, counting steps
tiles under a chosen count are the hot path
optionally, turn every tile beyond a second count to wall
```

The talk’s author finds the route, makes a Dijkstra map from all of its points, and takes everything under a value of, say, 10 {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s258" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s259" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}. The demo then culls at 15, so a band of floor survives beyond the hot path it shows {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L154" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Caves, hot path cull: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "hot-path", demos: ["c20-hot-path"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0016-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0016-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 16 of 18." at=16 of=18 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0017-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0017-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 17 of 18." key="hot-path.marked" at=17 of=18 %}
A second Dijkstra map starts from every tile of the route at once, so each tile’s value is its distance from the route. Tiles under a set distance, 10 in the demo, are the hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L145" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s260" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s261" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s262" /%}. The radius: {% value %}10{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c20-0018-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c20-0018-dark.png" alt="Caves, hot path cull, seed 1: the map at step 18 of 18." key="hot-path.culled" at=18 of=18 %}
Tiles at the cull distance or farther from the route become wall. The talk’s demo culls at 15, wider than the 10 of its hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L154" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s263" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s264" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. The cull distance: {% value %}15{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c20-hot-path.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
- `radius` (1 to 1,000; the talk’s: `10`) {% own /%}. Tiles fewer than this many steps from the route are the hot path {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L131-L145" /%}. The lab’s walk also keeps its caches at least this far from the route {% own /%}.
- `cull` (0 to 1,000; the talk’s: `15`) {% own /%}. Tiles this many steps or more from the route become wall {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c20-hot-path/src/main.rs#L147-L154" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L12-L16" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-code/backend/src/lib.rs#L54-L65" /%}. At 0 nothing is culled {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it produces, measured" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.hot-path" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: The hot path" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Caves, hot path cull (c20)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.311, 0.278 to 0.339 {% mark p10=0.278 median=0.311 p90=0.339 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
* 1, 1 to 1 {% mark p10=1 median=1 p90=1 unit="seeds" to=60 trait="regions" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="regions" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Dead ends](#our-definitions)
* 53.5, 43 to 62 {% mark p10=43 median=53.5 p90=62 unit="seeds" to=140 trait="dead_ends" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="dead_ends" digits=0 /%}
---
* [Corridor ratio](#our-definitions)
* 0.130, 0.107 to 0.152 {% mark p10=0.107 median=0.13 p90=0.152 unit="seeds" to=0.4 trait="corridor_ratio" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="corridor_ratio" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Path](#our-definitions)
* 102, 92 to 113.1 {% mark p10=92 median=102 p90=113.1 unit="seeds" to=290 trait="path" series="c20-hot-path" /%}
* {% now trait="path" digits=0 /%}
{% /table %}

The cull at 15 keeps about half the floor: a share of 0.311 at the median against 0.627 before it, on a route of the same 102 steps {% own-run values="c20.floor_share.median c18.floor_share.median c20.path.median" /%}. The talk offers it for a less branchy game, one that doesn’t make the player explore winding labyrinths with no purpose {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s263" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s264" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s265" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s266" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Where it fails" %}
No seed from 0 to 199 fails any of [our criteria](#what-counts-as-failing) {% own-run values="list.fails.hot-path" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it combines with" %}
The talk’s demos that run it with other stages {% own /%}:

- [cellular → cull → start → exit → hot-path](#) `c20`: the hot path

The lab’s walk hides its caches off the hot path, by [a rule of our own](#the-walk) {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Checked against the talk’s code" %}
Our stage against the talk’s own code, each run on seeds 0 to 199 and [measured the same way](#is-this-the-talks-technique) {% own-run values="list.checked.hot-path" /%}:

- `c20-hot-path`: 8 of 8 traits consistent with the talk’s own code.
{% /part %}

{% /card %}

{% card title="Hot rooms" id="hot-rooms" kind="Analysis" %}
On a map of rooms, the route says which rooms a player has to pass through and which are optional {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s267" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s268" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p30" /%}.

Stage `hot-rooms`. The talk’s demo: `c21-hot-rooms`.

{% part title="The rule" %}
```text
find the route from the start to the exit
a room is on the route if any step of the route is inside it
highlight those rooms, and gray the rest
```

The talk’s uses for the gray rooms: cull them for a room-to-room game, or hide bonus things in them {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s270" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s271" /%}. For the rooms on the route: order a story along them, since the player will probably pass through them in order {% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s274" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s275" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s276" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-slides/pdf#p31" /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="Step through it" %}
{% interactive id="lab" caption="Step through Rooms, hot rooms: seed 1, 80 by 50 tiles. Change the seed or a control and the map is built again." params={mode: "card", stage: "hot-rooms", demos: ["c21-hot-rooms"]} %}
{% steps %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c21-0072-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c21-0072-dark.png" alt="Rooms, hot rooms, seed 1: the map at step 72 of 73." at=72 of=73 %}
The map before the next step.
{% /step %}
{% step src="assets/steps/c21-0073-light.png" dark="assets/steps/c21-0073-dark.png" alt="Rooms, hot rooms, seed 1: the map at step 73 of 73." key="hot-rooms.marked" at=73 of=73 %}
A room is on the route when a step of the route falls inside it. The demo highlights those rooms and grays the rest {% cite id="wolverson2020-code/c21-hot-rooms/src/main.rs#L129-L156" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s267" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s268" /%}{% cite id="wolverson2020-talk/transcript#s269" /%}. Rooms on the route: {% value %}9{% /value %}.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

On the command line: `map-lab build recipes/c21-hot-rooms.json`.
{% /interactive %}
{% /part %}

{% part title="Controls" %}
This stage has no controls. It reads the rooms and the route that the stages before it made {% own /%}.
{% /part %}

{% part title="What it produces, measured" %}
Seeds 0 to 199, our own runs: the median, then the range 8 of 10 seeds fall in {% own-run values="table.measured.hot-rooms" /%}.

{% table label="Measured traits: Hot rooms" rowheads=true key=true %}
* Trait
* Rooms, hot rooms (c21)
* This map
---
* [Floor share](#our-definitions)
* 0.248, 0.212 to 0.279 {% mark p10=0.212 median=0.248 p90=0.279 unit="seeds" to=1 trait="floor_share" series="c21-hot-rooms" /%}
* {% now trait="floor_share" digits=3 /%}
---
* [Regions](#our-definitions)
